## 🏗️ Architecture Patterns

### Theme Architecture

```
themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/
├── assets/
│   ├── scripts/          → JS modules, classes
│   ├── styles/           → SCSS (BEM structure)
│   └── public/           → Static assets
├── blocks/src/blocks/    → Gutenberg blocks
├── classes/              → PHP classes (Composer autoload)
│   ├── Admin/            → Bootstrapping, initialization
│   ├── Base/             → Abstract base classes, traits
│   ├── Blocks/           → Block registration
│   ├── Database/         → Custom tables, migrations
│   ├── Endpoints/        → REST API endpoints
│   ├── PostTypes/        → Custom post types
│   ├── Taxonomies/       → Custom taxonomies
│   └── Users/            → User management
├── docs/                 → Complete documentation
├── inc/                  → Helper functions, loaders
├── sections/             → Reusable template parts
├── templates/            → Page templates
└── functions.php         → Theme entry point (minimal)
```

### Class Loading

**Pattern:** All classes extend `Base` and use `Singleton` trait. Initialization happens in `Admin::load_instances()`.

```php
// Example: Creating a new class
class MyClass extends Base {
    use Singleton;
    
    public function init(): void {
        parent::init();
        // Your initialization
    }
    
    public function register_actions(): void {
        $this->add_action('hook_name', 'method_name');
    }
}
```

**Reference:** [`themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/docs/class-loading-architecture.md`](themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/docs/class-loading-architecture.md)

### REST API Endpoints

Endpoints extend `BaseEndpoint` and register via `rest_api_init` hook:

```php
class MyEndpoint extends BaseEndpoint {
    public function register_routes(): void {
        register_rest_route('tcm/v1', '/my-resource', [
            'methods' => 'POST',
            'callback' => [$this, 'handle_request'],
            'permission_callback' => [$this, 'permission'],
        ]);
    }
}
```

**Key endpoints:**
- `POST /tcm/v1/booking-session` — Create checkout session
- `POST /tcm/v1/booking/prebook` — TBO PreBook (hold reservation)
- `POST /tcm/v1/booking/book` — TBO Book (confirm reservation)
- `GET /tcm/v1/booking/detail/{id}` — Get booking details
- `POST /tcm/v1/booking/cancel/{id}` — Cancel booking

**Reference:** [`themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/docs/endpoints-architecture.md`](themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/docs/endpoints-architecture.md)

### Database Migrations

Custom tables use `BaseTable` + `BaseMigration` pattern:

```php
// classes/Database/MyTable/Table.php
class MyTable extends BaseTable {
    protected $tableSlug = 'my_table';
}

// classes/Database/MyTable/Migration.php
class MyTableMigration extends BaseMigration {
    protected $tableSlug = 'my_table';
    protected $migrations = [
        ['version' => 2025010101, 'sql' => 'CREATE TABLE %s ...']
    ];
}
```

**Reference:** [`themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/docs/database-architecture.md`](themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/docs/database-architecture.md)

### Booking Session System

The **BookingSession** manages temporary state for hotel checkout flow:

```
Search → Create Session → PreBook → Book → BookingDetail
          ↓ session_id    ↓ BlockRoomId  ↓ BookingId
```

**Key identifiers:**
- `session_id` (UUID) — Local WordPress session (NOT sent to TBO)
- `BookingCode` — From TBO Search, identifies room option
- `BlockRoomId` — From TBO PreBook, holds reservation
- `BookingId` — From TBO Book, final confirmation

**Reference:** [`themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/docs/booking-session-architecture.md`](themes/travel-concierge-me-theme/docs/booking-session-architecture.md)

